From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:25:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] scl/mio/nf: load-aware mapping (PHYS-ABC P6): read_lib
 -l, &nf -l

read_lib -l derives a GENLIB from the NLDM liberty with EVERY drive
variant and per pin `UNKNOWN <cap fF> 999 <PD ps> <LD ps/fF> <PD> <LD>`
(Abc_SclComputeLoadDelayPin: tangent of the delay-vs-load row at the
average slew). Mio_Cell2_t carries iLDs/iCaps; Mio_CollectRootsNew2
keeps all variants in that mode (the truth-table dedup then applies only
to the const/buffer/inverter slots). &nf -l evaluates
PD + LD*load(root) + AvgLD*cap(pin) at the two cut-match arrival sites
and in Nf_CutRequired, from a per-node load vector: round 0 = flow refs
x average pin cap + the wire_load table by fanout count, later rounds =
input caps of the cells chosen for the fanouts, clamped at -X (30 fF).
The AvgLD*cap term is the logical-effort self-penalty: without it the
delay round picks maximal drives everywhere and the next round's loads
explode. SCL_GENLIB_DUMP=<file> writes the derived
GENLIB for inspection.

Stock paths are byte-identical (read_lib without -l, &nf without -l).
Note: a liberty without timing tables makes `read_lib -G` map on the
0.01 ps clamp; the load-aware genlib must come from an NLDM liberty.
On a cv64a6 group under the SCL STA without wires, &nf -l was much
faster than stock &nf, and than stock plus upsize/dnsize, with less
area (CEC-equivalent).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
